course: dictionary
lesson: 2027
title: Confinement: being kept in
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Confinement means being kept in a small space, or not being allowed to leave. Look at the words around it for clues. «"Administrative segregation" is the US official phrase for solitary confinement» tells you that solitary means alone, and the sentence adds that the prisoner is kept away from everyone, as a punishment.
explain: Solitary confinement is a phrase to learn. Read the clues: alone, away from everyone, as a punishment. Ask yourself what word would fit, then swap in your meaning, "kept alone in a cell", and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some words have an old meaning too. «"Confinement" means the time around giving birth (old-fashioned, mostly UK).» The word old-fashioned is a clue that people do not use it this way today. When a meaning seems strange, check a dictionary.
fact: Confinement means being kept in a small space, or not being allowed to leave.
fact: Solitary confinement means keeping a prisoner alone in a cell.
fact: Solitary confinement is called administrative segregation in the US.
fact: Old-fashioned: confinement was a polite word for the time a woman gives birth and rests in bed.
fact: Old-fashioned words can have meanings that people no longer use, so check the clues.
exercise: «The animals were in confinement.» What does confinement mean here? | Being given a big meal | *Being kept in a small space or not allowed to leave | Being free to run wherever they like | Being sent away to a faraway school
exercise: «Keeping a prisoner alone in a cell, away from everyone, as a punishment.» What does solitary confinement mean? | Giving a prisoner a party | *Keeping a prisoner alone in a cell | Keeping a prisoner with lots of friends | Letting a prisoner go home early
exercise: In «solitary confinement», which word is the clue that means alone? | cell | prisoner | *solitary | confinement
test: In an old book, a character says «Her confinement began in the spring.» What does confinement mean here? | A long holiday at the seaside | *The time around giving birth, when she rests in bed | Being sent to prison | Being given a new school
test: «The prisoner was kept in confinement.» What does this tell you about him? | He was at a party | He was very hungry | *He was kept where he could not leave | He was free to go out
exam: Maya reads «the bird was in confinement» and guesses it means flying high. What clue tells you she is wrong? | The word bird is short and easy | *Confinement means being kept in, not being free to fly | Flying is a happy word, so the bird must be happy | Birds always fly high, so that is not a clue
